  "summary": "The paper compares four vacuum-filtered Ti3C2Tx film electrodes: unsonicated TCS-0 and Ti3C2Tx sonicated for 1 h, 2 h, or 3 h (TCS-1, TCS-2, and TCS-3). All were produced by LiF/HCl etching of Ti3AlC2 followed by exfoliation; the variants differ only in ultrasonic fragmentation duration and resultant lateral sheet size. TCS-3 is the headline and best-performing electrode, reporting 658 F g\u22121 at 1 A g\u22121 in an H2SO4 aqueous electrolyte, versus 289 F g\u22121 for TCS-0 under the same condition. No numerical capacitance values for TCS-1 or TCS-2, film thicknesses, mass loadings per area, electrolyte concentration, or numerical interlayer spacings were printed; BET labels in the text conflict with the TCS labels."
}